title: Start
---
Villager: I am busy right now. Talk to the right worker if you need help.
===

title: Lumber
---
Lumber: You want passage on that boat? Then you need more than a spare board.
Lumber: The Sailor needs a reinforced Plank. It has to survive deep water, rocks, and whatever waits past the coast.
Lumber: I can make it, but only with 60 wood, 25 Stick, 12 iron, and 4 flaming_ore to burn the sealant in.
-> Why does the fisherman need that?
    Lumber: Normal boards split before the boat reaches open water. This Plank keeps the hull alive.
-> What will you give me?
    Lumber: The Plank. It is one of the two things the Sailor will demand before letting you aboard.
-> I will come back.
    Lumber: Come back with 60 wood, 25 Stick, 12 iron, and 4 flaming_ore. Anything less is not end-of-the-world work.
===

title: Miner
---
Miner: The Sailor still needs an Anchor strong enough for the deep current.
Miner: I can forge one, but not from common metal.
Miner: Bring me 15 diamond, 10 radium, 6 plasma, and 10 gold. Then I can make something that holds.
-> Why those materials?
    Miner: Diamond takes the pressure, gold carries the rune lines, radium hardens the Anchor, and plasma wakes it up.
-> What will you give me?
    Miner: The Anchor. The Sailor will not leave shore without it.
-> I will come back.
    Miner: Bring 15 diamond, 10 radium, 6 plasma, and 10 gold. If you are not ready for that, you are not ready for the sea.
===

title: Sailor
---
Sailor: My boat is not a ferry. Past the bay, the sea eats weak ships.
Sailor: If the Lumber made you the Plank, and the Miner forged the Anchor, then maybe you are worth taking.
Sailor: Bring me both: the Plank and the Anchor. Then I will let you aboard.
-> Why do you need both?
    Sailor: The Plank keeps the hull from breaking. The Anchor keeps the boat from being dragged into the dark water. Missing either one gets us killed.
-> I have work to do.
    Sailor: Then prove you are at the end of your journey. I sail only when both repairs are ready.
===
